# rules: cs-swallowed-errors
# languages: c_sharp
# fixture: csharp/SwallowedErrors.cs
#
# Where an exception is caught and nothing is done about it: an empty catch
# block, with or without an exception type. Not always wrong, but always a
# place where the code has decided a failure does not matter.
#
# It is found as text, because no pattern for a C# catch clause compiles to
# one - a snippet starting `try` is read as a call to something named catch.

scan_regex("*.cs"; "\\bcatch\\b\\s*(?:\\((?P<E>[\\w.]+)[^)]*\\))?\\s*(?:when\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\\s*)?\\{\\s*\\}")
| finding("cs-swallowed-errors"; "catches an exception and ignores it")
| report
